course: dictionary
lesson: 9740
title: Sunshade: keeping the sun off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sunshade is something that keeps the sun off you, like a big umbrella at the beach or a canopy over a garden table. The word is made of two smaller words, sun and shade, so the name itself gives you a clue.
explain: «Kites were flown in China at least by the 5th century BC and used for signals; sunshades and umbrellas were also known in ancient Egypt and Assyria.» The word «also» tells you that sunshades are in the same group as umbrellas. Umbrellas keep the sun and rain off you, so a sunshade must do something similar.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "sunshades were also known in ancient Egypt" with "something that keeps the sun off you" in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have it. Remember that a car sunshade is a screen on the windscreen, so one word can fit more than one place.
fact: A sunshade is something that keeps sunlight off you or off a place.
fact: A sunshade can be a big umbrella at the beach or a canopy over a garden table.
fact: A car sunshade is a screen on the windscreen that blocks sunlight and keeps the car cool.
fact: «Sunshades» and umbrellas were known in ancient Egypt and Assyria.
fact: Sunshades, hats and shade sails help protect your skin from the sun.
exercise: «Sunshades and umbrellas were also known in ancient Egypt and Assyria.» What is a sunshade? | A kind of boat that sails on the sea | A type of cold drink | A loud sound made by a kite | *Something that keeps the sun off you, like a big umbrella
exercise: Mum says, «Put the car sunshade up, it's boiling in here.» What does a car sunshade do? | *It blocks sunlight on the windscreen and keeps the car cool | It plays music | It makes the car go faster | It keeps the car dry in the rain
exercise: In «sunshades and umbrellas were also known», which word tells you sunshades are like umbrellas? | ancient | kites | Egypt | *also
test: Lena sits «under the sunshade» all afternoon. What does under the sunshade mean? | *In the shade of something that keeps the sun off | Inside a shop, out of the rain | Up a tree, high above the sand | In the sea, splashing about
test: Which of these is a sunshade? | *A canopy over a garden table | A cup of hot tea | A pair of running shoes | A bus ticket
exam: Why do families put up sunshades at the beach? | To call their friends over | To catch fish in the sea | To make the sand wet | *To keep the sun off them and stay cool
